# Changelog Format (Keep a Changelog 1.1)

`CHANGELOG.md` is for humans: curated notable changes, not a git log dump.

## Structure
- Newest version first; every version gets a section `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` (ISO 8601 date).
- Always keep an `## [Unreleased]` section at the top — every user-facing change lands there in the same change set that makes it.
- Group entries under exactly these headings (omit empty ones):
  - `### Added` — new features
  - `### Changed` — changes in existing functionality
  - `### Deprecated` — soon-to-be removed features
  - `### Removed` — removed features
  - `### Fixed` — bug fixes
  - `### Security` — vulnerabilities (lead with the CVE if there is one)
- Breaking changes and deprecations are never omitted; mark them clearly (**Breaking:** prefix) and note upgrade steps.
- Yanked releases stay listed: `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD [YANKED]`.
- Compare links at the bottom only if the file already uses them; keep the existing style of each file.
- Write for admins and users, not a git log. Anything an admin must do after updating (re-copy units, run a drush command, set a setting) goes in **bold** — the release skills turn those into manual steps.

## Release workflow
Before tagging a release:
1. Rename `[Unreleased]` content into a new `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section.
2. Re-create an empty `[Unreleased]` section above it.
3. Update the compare links at the bottom (if present).
4. Commit (`Release x.y.z.`), then create an annotated tag `x.y.z` — plain, never `vx.y.z`.

A tag must contain its rolled section: never tag a commit whose changelog still lists the changes under `[Unreleased]`.

## Template

```markdown
# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

## [1.0.0] - 2026-01-15

### Added

- Initial release.

[unreleased]: https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/compare/1.0.0...HEAD
[1.0.0]: https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/releases/tag/1.0.0
```
